# Comprehensive UI Maintenance & Performance Plan

This plan aims to resolve the reported modal unresponsiveness, the visual clipping in input fields, and to upgrade the aesthetics of the "Tour" icon to a premium standard.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - The inputs will have their leading padding reduced to prevent text from being hidden behind non-existent icons.
> - The "Tour" icon will be replaced with a premium Lighthouse design.
> - Global modal functions will be strictly enforced to clear inline styles that prevent closing.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Fix Input Field Clipping

#### [MODIFY] [ui-kit.css](file:///e:/2026%20SISTEMAS/2025%20Infra%20Sistemas%20YASMIN/ui-kit.css)
- Update `.form-group input`, `.form-group select`, and `.form-group textarea` (around line 507).
- Change `padding: 0.75rem 0.75rem 0.75rem 2.75rem` to `padding: 0.75rem 1rem`.
- Only add left padding if an icon is present (using a specific wrapper class if needed, or removing the global large padding).

### 2. Fix Modal Closing Logic

#### [MODIFY] [ui-kit.js](file:///e:/2026%20SISTEMAS/2025%20Infra%20Sistemas%20YASMIN/ui-kit.js)
- Update `closeModal(modalId)` to explicitly clear inline styles:
  ```javascript
  modal.style.display = 'none';
  modal.style.opacity = '0';
  modal.classList.remove('visible');
  ```
- Update `closeAllModals()` to do the same for all active modals and the `#overlay`.

### 3. Improve Tour Icon Aesthetics

#### [MODIFY] [index.html](file:///e:/2026%20SISTEMAS/2025%20Infra%20Sistemas%20YASMIN/index.html)
- Replace the SVG inside `button#global-tour-btn` (line 3717) with a premium Lighthouse SVG.
- Add a subtle pulse animation or hover effect to the button to make it feel "active" and helpful.

